# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Data & logs
pipeline.db
.auto-research-logs/
.cache/

# MacOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Claude Code — local state stays out, committed skills stay in
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Candidates (generated, not source)
.auto-research-candidates/

# meta_review Role-revision proposals (advisory, not source)
.role-proposals/

# A/B test runtime ledger
.ab_test/

# Local secrets — NEVER commit
.env
.env.*
.ctrader_tokens.json

# Live broker position state — per-host, never shipped in the image (a fresh
# volume must own nothing; see docker-entrypoint.sh)
fix_runner_state.json
# Trigger-driven scheduling (RUNNER_MODE=cron): the ask, and the receipt proving a pass
# ran. Both are per-host runtime state that lives on the mounted volume — shipping a
# stale trade_now in the image would make a fresh pod trade the moment it booted.
trade_now
last_pass.json

# swap_log.py stdout/stderr — the durable record is the broker_swap table in
# pipeline.db, never these files
.swap-logs/

# Runtime logs from the two books. Per-host and rotated; the durable per-bar
# record is the sleeve_equity table, not these.
.fix-logs/
.paper-trading-logs/

# Ad-hoc analysis output. Every one of these is REGENERATED by a command that
# lives in the repo (evaluate_strategy, causal_audit, the sweep scripts), so the
# command is the source and the file is a build artefact. Committing them also
# freezes a number that goes stale the moment the book changes — the exact
# failure the sleeve-ops "recompute, never quote" rule exists to prevent.
.eval-*.txt
.claude-top5-eval-spec.txt
.top4-*.txt
.top5-*.txt
.kelly-sweep.log
.kelly-up-sweep.log
.lookahead-sweep.log
.lookahead-sweep.json
.stress-realsized.log
_queue_sweep.log
causal_audit.csv
shadow_diff.csv
nnfx_audit_results.json

# Local research databases. pipeline.db is already ignored above; these are the
# same class. macro_data.db is a local cache (the pod has neither it nor a
# FRED key by design), and strategies/strategy_results/trials are leftovers from
# an abandoned split — see the 2026-07-28 decision against a second DB file.
macro_data.db
strategies.db
strategy_results.db
trials.db

# Per-host runtime state, same reasoning as fix_runner_state.json above.
# Glob, not the bare name: there is one state file PER VENUE
# (prop_guard_state_ctrader.json), and the un-globbed pattern left the PROP
# account's drawdown anchors — start_nav, the midnight base, the peak — untracked
# but committable. Shipping one into the image would hand a fresh volume a stale
# base to measure a 3% daily limit against.
prop_guard_state*.json

# graphify knowledge-graph output — generated from the repo, rebuilt on demand
graphify-out/

# Academic anomaly rotation cursor — per-host generation state, not source. It
# only records how far the walk has advanced; committing it would rewind or jump
# another host's rotation for no benefit. Losing it costs coverage briefly (the
# walk restarts at 0 and re-converges), never correctness.
.academic_rotation

# .scratch mixes DESIGN NOTES that belong in history with THROWAWAY RUN OUTPUT that
# does not. The convention is already established by what is tracked: all 16 tracked
# files under .scratch are .md. So keep markdown, drop the rest — 22M of .pkl sleeve
# caches were sitting untracked in .scratch/costed alone, and a repo whose .git had
# already ballooned to 33GB once (2026-08-05) should not be offered them.
.scratch/**
!.scratch/**/
!.scratch/**/*.md
